  fit: {mode: fill}
notes: |
  Timing: about 55 seconds.

  I chose Las Meninas because it disrupted the fast, classificatory way I had learned to look at art. As a child, I entered pictures slowly through books and illustrations. Later I began to identify the subject, period, and style, then move on. Las Meninas resisted that habit. The painter, the enormous canvas, the mirror, the rear doorway, and several outward gazes all make my own position part of the composition. I was no longer only looking at a painting; the painting seemed to organize the place from which I looked.
